#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:2
msgid "How the pieces fit"
msgstr "各部分如何配合"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:5
msgid "One loop, several useful boundaries"
msgstr "一个循环，几条有用的边界"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:7
msgid "An agent alternates model calls and tool execution until it has a final answer. Providers, tools, and extensions supply the capabilities around that loop. Your application can adopt them separately without adopting a web server, UI, or another application's data model."
msgstr "智能体在模型调用和工具执行之间交替，直到得出最终答案。模型提供商、工具和扩展为这个循环提供各种能力。你的应用可以单独采用它们，而不必同时采用一套 Web 服务器、UI 或另一个应用的数据模型。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:26
msgid "Who owns what"
msgstr "谁拥有什么"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:32
msgid "Object"
msgstr "对象"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:33
msgid "Responsibility"
msgstr "职责"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:34
msgid ":class:`~zett_agent.agent.Agent`"
msgstr ":class:`~zett_agent.agent.Agent`"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:35
msgid "Admits requests, runs the model/tool loop, cleans up."
msgstr "接收请求，运行模型/工具循环，并负责清理。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:36
msgid ":class:`~zett_agent.client.AgentClient`"
msgstr ":class:`~zett_agent.client.AgentClient`"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:37
msgid "Convenient creation and event handling; exposes the runtime as ``client.agent``."
msgstr "提供便捷的创建方式和事件处理；把运行时暴露为 ``client.agent``\\ 。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:38
msgid ":class:`~zett_agent.model.AgentModel`"
msgstr ":class:`~zett_agent.model.AgentModel`"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:39
msgid "Talks to one provider and normalizes its stream."
msgstr "与某一个模型提供商通信，并把它的流式输出规范化。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:40
msgid ":class:`~zett_agent.agent.AgentRunContext`"
msgstr ":class:`~zett_agent.agent.AgentRunContext`"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:41
msgid "Per-request state shared with extensions; use it instead of global state."
msgstr "与扩展共享的请求级状态；请使用它，而不是全局状态。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:42
msgid ":class:`~zett_agent.extensions.base.AgentExtension`"
msgstr ":class:`~zett_agent.extensions.base.AgentExtension`"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:43
msgid "Optional behavior at documented hooks; defaults do nothing."
msgstr "在文档列出的钩子上提供可选行为；默认什么都不做。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:44
msgid ":class:`~zett_agent.dispatcher.AgentEventDispatcher`"
msgstr ":class:`~zett_agent.dispatcher.AgentEventDispatcher`"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:45
msgid "Your callbacks for a stream; it never injects context or runs tools."
msgstr "你在某条流上的回调；它从不注入上下文，也不运行工具。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:48
msgid "Composition, not a second runtime"
msgstr "是组合，不是第二个运行时"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:50
msgid "``create_agent`` wraps an Agent; it does not create a different loop. You can use :class:`~zett_agent.agent.Agent` directly with ``async for``, wrap an existing Agent in a client, and add behavior through extensions without subclassing the Agent."
msgstr "``create_agent`` 只是包装了一个 Agent，并不会创建另一套循环。你可以直接对\\ :class:`~zett_agent.agent.Agent`\\ 使用 ``async for``，把已有的 Agent 包装进客户端，并通过扩展添加行为，而无需继承 Agent。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:55
msgid "Your application owns the resources it passes in. The runtime closes the streams it opens, but it never closes a provider or database you supplied — release those yourself when the application shuts down."
msgstr "你的应用拥有自己传入的资源。运行时只关闭自己打开的流，但绝不会关闭你提供的模型提供商或数据库——这些资源要在应用关闭时由你自己释放。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:60
msgid "Which boundary should I use?"
msgstr "该用哪条边界？"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:62
msgid "Use a provider adapter to connect an endpoint, not to manage conversation history."
msgstr "用模型适配器连接端点，而不是用它管理对话历史。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:63
msgid "Use a tool for an operation the model may request, not a second model loop."
msgstr "对模型可能请求的操作要用工具，而不是再套一层模型循环。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:64
msgid "Use an extension for context, permissions, persistence, or behavior during a request."
msgstr "用扩展处理上下文、权限、持久化，或请求过程中的行为。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:65
msgid "Use a dispatcher for presentation and telemetry that only observe UI events."
msgstr "用分发器处理只观察 UI 事件的呈现和遥测。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:67
msgid "For example, a review assistant can compose a provider, read-only tools, project guidance, and session storage. Its UI displays the resulting events without needing to know how those capabilities are implemented. See :doc:`../learn/configuration` for composition and :doc:`../extending/first-extension` when the built-ins do not cover your workflow."
msgstr "例如，一个代码评审助手可以组合模型提供商、只读工具、项目指令和会话存储。它的 UI 只需展示产生的事件，不必知道这些能力是如何实现的。组合方式见\\ :doc:`../learn/configuration`；内置扩展不覆盖你的工作流时，请见\\ :doc:`../extending/first-extension`\\ 。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:74
msgid "Limits and safety"
msgstr "限制与安全"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:76
msgid "``max_iterations`` caps model calls per user or internal input. Tool round trips consume that budget."
msgstr "``max_iterations`` 限制每条用户输入或内部输入能触发的模型调用次数。工具往返会消耗这个额度。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:78
msgid "``max_internal_messages`` caps queued internal continuations in one request."
msgstr "``max_internal_messages`` 限制一次请求中排队的 internal continuation 数量。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:79
msgid "Neither limit is a spending cap or a permission boundary."
msgstr "这两个限制都不是花费上限，也不是权限边界。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:81
msgid "Filesystem, shell, and MCP tools run with the permissions of your process or server. Tool guidance is documentation, not enforcement. Guard untrusted input with explicit allow-lists, approval rules, resource limits, and process isolation."
msgstr "文件系统、shell 和 MCP 工具以你的进程或服务器的权限运行。工具 guidelines 只是说明，不是强制约束。请用显式的允许列表、审批规则、资源限制和进程隔离来防护不可信的输入。"

#: ../../concepts/architecture.rst:86
msgid "Next: :doc:`lifecycle` for the exact order of hooks inside one request."
msgstr "下一步：看\\ :doc:`lifecycle`，了解一次请求内部钩子的确切顺序。"

